# Line endings, settled once.
#
# Without this, every file authored on Windows is stored with CRLF, and the moment the repo
# is opened on macOS git reports every one of them as entirely rewritten. Diffs become
# useless and merges conflict on whitespace. `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository
# and checks out LF everywhere — which is also what Node, pnpm and every tool in this stack
# expect.
#
# Applied to the existing history with `git add --renormalize .`, so the 19 files already
# stored with CRLF are fixed rather than left as a trap for the first Mac checkout.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF regardless of platform: a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter with a trailing carriage return and fail with a baffling error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries. Marking these explicitly stops git from ever attempting line-ending conversion
# on them, which silently corrupts the file.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and excluded from language statistics — reviewing a
# lockfile line by line is never the point.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff

# Playwright visual baselines are platform-specific renderings, not source. Never diffed.
e2e/**/*-snapshots/** binary linguist-generated=true
